  "question": "X2, rule T refit 2 (the last, lead's ruling: the same formula reaching 9 wide), fresh round, plus the 3 wide read again clear of the section toolbar. A lone Shape on the right margin track, pressed 10% in from its left, held and moved +1, then left, ring read at each, twice (R1, R2): 9 wide (lines 18 to 27) at 1600 and 1760 at points not read before; 6 wide at 1545 (margin track 1.05 columns) and 1672 (2.13); 3 wide on rows 8 to 14, lines 24 to 27, at 1600 (ours' read table, inferred for 3 wide; scored apart from T). Blocks Probe, unsaved, one block per enter.",
  "rule": "T refit 2: a lone 6 or 9 wide on the right margin track, its box (width - 1) columns plus that track (M, K = M / pitch). With K under 1 it takes the left edge rule from the first pixel. Otherwise, with n = width - 1 + round(K): a move left is on 27 - (n + 2) until -(M / 2 + 5), then on 27 - (n + 1), or the left edge rule's column when that is further left (out to column 1); a move right goes to 27 - (width - 1 + ceil((M - 12) / pitch)). 9 wide takes the left edge rule, not the mirror.",
  "from": "Ours with refit 2 (editor.js updateMove on branch x2-t-refit2), each ring from mid-check's hold sweep at that frame width (viewport by 945). Seen: 75 of 75 rings (CAP-X2SIX.json A, CAP-X2TWIDTHS.json, CAP-X2TREFIT.json, CAP-X2W39.json 9 wide, the last read in an overlapped session). asBuilt: ours on main (refit 1, 9 wide on the mirror table). Points sit away from both rules' steps.",
  "hit": "Each case's two ring reads must agree; then the ring must equal refit 2's ('ring'). T's count is the w9 and w6 cases; the w3 cases are ours' table ('table'), scored apart. A start not on its area, or the block not selected, is a setup miss, named, not scored. Two reads that disagree are named unsteady. T freezes after this round whatever it scores; refit 2 is built only if it beats asBuilt on these reads.",
